<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chełm</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kholm</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chełm is a city in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, near the Ukrainian border. Founded as Kholm by Daniel of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a> in the 1230s, it became his capital and burial place, and it passed to Poland in the 14th century. It is known for the chalk tunnels beneath its old town and its cathedral hill.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chelm.jpg" alt="Chełm" width="320" height="438" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Akna · CC BY-SA 3.0 pl · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Che%C5%82m,_Bazylika_NNMP.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
